---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { storyInNav } from '../data/story';
---

<Base
  title="Story"
  description="A later timeline of Radin Khayyam’s path into research, including the years he competed in table tennis."
  noindex={!storyInNav}
>
  <header class="page-head">
    <h1>Story</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      A later timeline will go here, including the path from competition into research. It is not in the navigation yet.
    </p>
  </header>
  <section class="block">
    <p>
      The network on the home page already reads its nodes from <code>src/data/network.ts</code>. Nodes can carry a
      milestone, a date, and a link. When this timeline is written, those fields are the entry points, and
      <code>storyInNav</code> in <code>src/data/story.ts</code> is the switch that adds the page to the nav and the
      sitemap.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
